implementationPlan.description:
THE SECURITY ARMS (DoD 2, 3, 5) - `apps/daemon/src/http/preview-read.test.ts`. ONE ARM PER REFUSAL CLASS, each asserting the CODE, never merely that it failed.

TRAVERSAL AND ESCAPE, each its own arm with its own code:
- `..` segments;
- an ABSOLUTE path;
- ENCODED separators (`%2e%2e%2f`, `%2f`, double-encoded) - the encoding guard exists precisely because a decode-then-check order lets these through;
- a SYMLINK inside the root pointing OUTSIDE it - assert against the RESOLVED path, since this is the case a pre-resolution check passes;
- a path INSIDE the root IS served (without this, an arm that refuses everything passes every case above).

TYPE CONFINEMENT (DoD 3): a `.sqlite`, a `.json` and a DOTFILE inside the root each refuse `LISTENER_ASSET_TYPE_UNKNOWN`. The previews root can sit beside real stores and receipts, so this is the arm that separates a confined image server from a general file server.

NO LEAK (DoD 5), WITH A POSITIVE CONTROL so it cannot pass vacuously: assert the served JSON contains no absolute host path, no credential, no url with embedded userinfo - and prove the assertion can fail by feeding it a value that SHOULD trip it. An absence assertion with no positive control is the classic vacuous arm.
Also assert a refusal body names the CODE and does NOT contain the resolved path it refused.

DoD 1's values are asserted against a receipt written by the REAL preview path, not a hand-built one.

THE MUTATION DRILL (DoD 6) - it proves the confinement is load-bearing rather than decorative.

REMOVE THE ROOT-CONFINEMENT CHECK from the capture route and confirm the traversal arm goes RED. QUOTE THE FAILING LINE. A confinement that has never been seen fail is not evidence, and this is the one boundary in the row whose silent failure is an exfiltration surface.

Drill the TYPE check the same way: allow any file type and confirm the `.sqlite`/`.json`/dotfile arms go red. DoD 3 treats directory and type as one confinement, so both halves need the drill.

RESTORE PER GLOBAL RAIL 13, which is stricter than the usual restore:
1. `git status --porcelain` the exact mutated paths FIRST;
2. back EVERY mutated path up OUT OF TREE (%TEMP%, suffixed by your worker id);
3. restore FROM THE BACKUP - not `git checkout --`;
4. prove by SHA256 equality in a call SEPARATE from the restore. A PowerShell copy can silently no-op, and "the command returned" is not evidence the bytes moved.
The new files are UNTRACKED, so `git diff` certifies nothing for them - the backup is the only proof.
